    The saturation falsification test for the 5-step curve's ratio decay (jl_performance/README.md, 'Hypothesis'). Same circuit family, same observable Z_62 and theta_zz = -pi/2, but 20 Trotter steps instead of 5 — 5420 channels (20 x (127 rx + 144 ZZ)) — so that ~2-3e6 terms is far from the reachable Pauli set's closure instead of at it. If the ratio keeps rising with the term count and jl's per-term cost stays flat, the decay was a saturation regime; if it decays here too, it is a large-m property of this engine. Benchmark C's angle and depth, whose 5420 per-layer counts it already proved identical at 2^-14.
